# Condition 3 — switchExpression destination parameter (P08 gate review, REPORT §6)

**Verdict: implemented and verified. The change is behaviour-preserving on every
measured input, because the Haxe typer already stamps the owning contract onto
the switch node at every probed site — so the in-scope derivation and the
carried contract always render identically today. No reachable divergence was
found; that is the result, not a gap in the measurement.**

Deliverables: this `REPORT.md`, `PATCH.diff` (4 logical changes, applies
cleanly with `patch -p0` against
`dc-warn/swc-try-fix-wt/wt/packages/compiler/reflaxe/swift/swiftcompiler/SwiftExpr.hx`,
sha256 `bf7dde2c…78`, and reproduces the tested file byte-for-byte), raw logs
and generated trees under `evidence/`.

Honesty framing, per the review's own §6 wording: the review observed **no
divergence** in its 11 instrumented generations, and this condition rests on
the obligation-1 wording ("in-scope reconstruction is removed"), not on a
demonstrated failure. The work below therefore does not dress unchanged output
as a bug fix: the expected common case is byte-identical output, and the
evidence section separates (a) the removal itself, (b) byte-identity where the
derived type was already right, and (c) the attempted construction of a wrong
case, which the typer makes unreachable.

